ll/windows). |\n| **`flutter_linux...tar.xz`** | ❌ *Not on GitHub* | 1.4 GB Linux Flutter zip. Won't work on Windows. |\n| **`Public` & `Templates`** | ❌ *Not on GitHub* | Completely empty Ubuntu default folders (0 bytes). |\n| **`snap`** | ❌ *Not on GitHub* | Ubuntu Snap runtime data. Snap is an Ubuntu-only packaging format. |\n| **`venv`** | ❌ *Not on GitHub* | Linux Python virtual environment (contains compiled Linux `.so` binaries). You recreate your venv on Windows with `python -m venv venv`. |\n| **`java_error...log`** | ❌ *Not on GitHub* | Old crash log text file from Android Studio. |\n| **`Ubuntu_Backup`** | — | This is the local folder where your backup was prepared before pushing to GitHub! |\n\n---\n\n### 💡 Why `StudioProjects` and `STM32CubeIDE` look different on GitHub:\nIn GitHub, when a folder only contains one subfolder, GitHub automatically displays them combined on a single line:\n- `StudioProjects/chat_bot_financial_trading`\n- `STM32CubeIDE/workspace_2.1.1`\n\nBoth contain all your project source code!\n\n---\n\n### Summary\nNone of your work or personal data was skipped. The only folders not on GitHub are **Linux-only software engines/SDKs** that cannot run on Windows and must be downloaded as Windows installers anyway.","thinking":"The environment appears to be a standard Python virtual environment, specifically created for Python 3.12. The `Ubuntu_Backup` directory contains a Git clone of a public repository.\n\n\n"}
